<title>UK: Racal shares down on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Racal shares down on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Racal Electronics Plc fell on Monday as investors took profits after a sharp rise on Friday, traders said.</p>
<p>The stock was down eight pence at 260-1/2 by 1209 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;It's just reversed Friday's gain. Late on Friday a couple of brokers chased each other round and drove the price up about 20p in as many minutes,&quot; one market-maker said.</p>
<p>Racal's share price reached 268-1/2p on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Paul Carrel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8958</p>
</text>
